  {
   "id": "8hRO01BKlywJ",
   "from": "Yihui Xie",
   "author": "cc1ef8c8158d6b73",
   "date": "2014-09-04T18:20:12Z",
   "subject": "Re: [shinyapps-users] How do I upload documentation?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "I think the easiest thing for you to do is to put help/index.html\r<br>under the www directory of your app. This file is probably not missing\r<br>on ShinyApps, but the link does not work because shiny does not allow\r<br>arbitrary links without pre-registering the URL prefix (see\r<br>?shiny::addResourcePath).\r<br>\r<br>Regards,\r<br>Yihui\r<br>--\r<br>Yihui Xie &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">xiey...@gmail.com</a>&gt;\r<br>Web: <a href=\"http://yihui.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://yihui.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792362459532000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1-cfF7XkDHIa_7Rv0NAY1j\">http://yihui.name</a>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>On Thu, Sep 4, 2014 at 1:02 PM,  &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">cust...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hello everyone!\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I&#39;m a little confused about how the function &quot;deployApp()&quot; understands the\r<br>&gt; borders of the app to upload. In my ui.R file, I have a link to\r<br>&gt; help/index.html (my slidified doc file), made with\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; tags$a(href=&quot;help/index.html&quot;, &quot;Read the Documentation!&quot;),\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; But, when I try and click, the link is broken, because the html file is\r<br>&gt; missing on the Shinyapp server.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; How should that work?\r<br>&gt; Or I&#39;m just not supposed to upload on shinyapp any non-shinyapp file?\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Thank you in advance.\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
